# Code owners for healthkey-ai/promop.
#
# Purpose is SOC2 CC8.1 change management: an auditor asks who reviews changes to
# security-relevant code, and this file is the answer that GitHub enforces rather
# than a convention people remember. Paths below are ordered least- to
# most-specific; the LAST matching pattern wins, so the security paths at the
# bottom override the catch-all at the top.
#
# This file only requests review. It becomes a control once branch protection on
# `dev` and `main` requires review from code owners — see issue #752.

# Default owner for everything not matched below.
*                                   @adamblum

# ── Authorization and identity ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every P0 finding in the security audit lived in one of these paths.
/omop_core/authorization.py         @adamblum
/patient_portal/api/permissions.py  @adamblum
/patient_portal/api/authentication.py  @adamblum
/patient_portal/api/providers/      @adamblum
/patient_portal/services.py         @adamblum
/patient_portal/api/break_glass.py  @adamblum

# ── Deployment, configuration and secrets ─────────────────────────────────────
# Changes here alter what runs in production or what guards it.
/ctomop/settings.py                 @adamblum
/patient_portal/checks.py           @adamblum
/start.sh                           @adamblum
/Dockerfile                         @adamblum
/Dockerfile.gcp                     @adamblum
/requirements.txt                   @adamblum

# ── CI and the security gates themselves ──────────────────────────────────────
# A change that weakens a gate should be as visible as a change that trips it.
/.github/                           @adamblum
/.gitleaks.toml                     @adamblum
/.bandit-baseline.json              @adamblum
